Description: Share the JPS and MPF descriptor codec with metadata-only picture saves
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Origin: vendor
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-11-12

diff --git a/docs/jps.md b/docs/jps.md
index f8b0642..6b8e549 100644
--- a/docs/jps.md
+++ b/docs/jps.md
@@ -35,3 +35,8 @@ The shared picture engine removes a declared separation when taking out the two
 
 The writer tests inspect each APP3 independently and reopen every successful write.
 They cover both orders, mono display choices, all four half-size flag combinations, separation including 255, comments, and refusals that leave the device bytes untouched.
+
+The descriptor codec is supplied by `libstereo-policy >= 1.17.5` (`stereo-jpeg.h`), shared with
+`Stereo::Picture::saveCorrection`. The plugin uses it for JPS payloads and MPF directories;
+metadata-only corrections never re-encode either JPEG image. Applications call the shared save
+entry point after the person's acceptance instead of assembling descriptor bytes themselves.
